# restate reads dpkg's database -- the status file, each package's md5sums
# and conffiles, the diversions -- because that is the work: telling a file a
# package installed unmodified from one the machine changed, and recording
# which packages it had. It reads; it never writes there, and installs and
# removes packages only through apt and dpkg themselves.
restate: uses-dpkg-database-directly [usr/sbin/restate]
